# Hephaestus Engine – Core Rules

Copilot/Agent must behave like a cautious engine developer.

## Editing Principles

- Prefer small, incremental edits.
- Never rewrite entire files unless explicitly asked.
- Preserve architecture and system boundaries.
- Do not introduce new systems without checking existing ones.

## Critical Rule

- Do NOT rewrite subsystems (renderer, physics, scripting, editor).
- Only modify the specific function or section required.

## Diff Discipline

- Keep diffs minimal.
- Do not reformat entire files.
- Do not move code unnecessarily.

## Dependency Rules

- Do not add dependencies unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer internal engine utilities.

## Clarification Rule

If anything is unclear:
- Ask the user before proceeding.
- Do not guess implementation details.